 1.  **Advection:** Move the fluid quantities (velocity and volume field) along the velocity field $\mathbf{u}_{t-1}$ [S1, unofficial]. This is performed by back-tracing particle positions using $\mathbf{u}_{t-1}$ and interpolating quantities from the source cells to the current cell [S1, unofficial].
-2.  **Force Application:** Add the external force to the advected velocity field [S1, unofficial]. The intermediate velocity is computed as $\mathbf{u}^* = \mathbf{u}_{\text{advected}} + \Delta t \cdot \mathbf{f}$ [G].
-3.  **Pressure Projection:** Rectify $\mathbf{u}^*$ to make it divergence-free ($\nabla \cdot \mathbf{u}_t = 0$) [S1, unofficial]. This involves solving for pressure $p$ such that $\nabla^2 p = \frac{1}{\Delta t} \nabla \cdot \mathbf{u}^*$, then updating the velocity as $\mathbf{u}_t = \mathbf{u}^* - \Delta t \nabla p$ [G].
